NanoChess
====================
A small C23 chess engine with an elo rating of around 2640. With a
compiled size of just under 81KB, there is no bloat or external
dependencies and it easily fits onto a floppy disk. It can be compiled on
almost any architecture such as amd64, arm64, PowerPC and i386.

No huge neural networks or weight files are used. Instead, NanoChess has a
pure classical handcrafted evaluation function. This uses PeSTO piece square
tables along with pawn structure, piece mobility curves, outpost,
tactical, king safety and tempo terms. As no matrix multiplication is used
or any neural functions, the evaluation is pretty quick.

The search function is an Alpha-Beta Negamax engine with Principal
Variation Search. It uses many modern tournament features such as Aspiration
windows, 1 ply & 2 ply continuation history, Singular Extensions, Multi-Cut
pruning, Adaptive Late Move Reductions and Null-Move Pruning. Check
evasion and Static Exchange pruning is used in the quiescence search.

Multi-threading is supported using a Lockless Lazy SMP engine. It can run
using between 1 and 64 threads.

The engine is easy to use with any UCI interface such as En Croissant,
Arena, Cutechess and Banksia. The Hash size is configurable between 1 and
1024MB (Default 32MB). The number of Threads can be set. OwnBook can be
toggled and Move Overhead adjusted. To compile the engine just run build.bat
on Windows or cmake on Linux/macOS.
